
# ssh-login

Automatic `ssh` login TTY on bootup

## usage

```shell
stow -Rv bash ssh-login
```

### systemd login

```shell
sudo systemctl edit getty@tty4
```

**NOTE:** Replace the username -- `jeff` -- in the following override snippet
with your user name.

```shell
# getty@tty4 override
[Service]
Environment="USE_SSH_LOGIN_TTY=1"
ExecStart=
ExecStart=-/sbin/agetty -o '-f -p -- jeff' --noissue --autologin jeff %I $TERM
```

